  "body": "## What happens\n\nPR #4490 (#4484) adds a menu bar over the ribbon. The dock is now about 24 px lower.\n\nAt a window of 1280 x 720, the viewport Display menu does not fit above its Display button. The menu is an `egui::Area` with its bottom on the button top (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/display_menu.rs`). egui keeps the area inside the screen, so the menu moves down and covers the button.\n\nPR #4490 runs `page_layout_windows::layout_window_display_menu` at 1366 x 768 (the smallest screen of the plan #4245). At that size the menu fits.\n\n## Expected\n\nAt 1280 x 720 the Display menu also stays above its button. For example, the menu gets a vertical scroll area with a maximum height (the space above the button), or it opens beside the button when the space above is too small.\n\n## Done means\n\n- At 1280 x 720 and at 1366 x 768, the Display menu does not cover the Display button.\n- `layout_window_display_menu` checks both sizes.\n",
